From 8ff5dc2c3208b164ba59004e9d365fa0770d8e1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tron <tron@tsmconsultz.dev>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 05:17:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: chain-status-bar in 5 war rooms pointed at unused
 TSM_RELAY_PAYLOAD key

The chain-status-bar widget (copy-pasted across legal, RE, insurance,
BPO, and construction war rooms) was reading a generic RELAY_KEY =
'TSM_RELAY_PAYLOAD' localStorage key that none of the war rooms
actually write to, so the bar always showed 'no relay yet' even after
a real escalation fired.

Fixed each war room to point at its real relay key:
- legal: TSM_LEGAL_WAR_RELAY (storeSession)
- RE: TSM_RE_WAR_RELAY (escalateToStrategist)
- insurance: tsm_ins_war_relay (storeRelay, lowercase as written)
- BPO: TSM_BPO_WAR_RELAY (storeWarRoomRelay)
- construction: TSM_CONSTRUCTION_WAR_RELAY (storeSession)

Also fixed a second bug in the same widget: all five payloads store
timestamp as new Date().toISOString() (a string), but the widget did
Date.now() - (d.timestamp || 0), which coerces the ISO string to NaN,
so 'age' was always NaN and the bar fell through to the stale-relay
branch even on a fresh relay. Now the timestamp is parsed to an epoch
number before the subtraction regardless of whether it's a string or
a number.

Follow-up (not in this commit): insurance and BPO have no code path
that ever writes TSM_STRAT_CONFIRMED_* / TSM_EXEC_CONFIRMED_* keys, so
their chain bars can reach 'Strategist receiving' but never advance to
'confirmed' state. That's a missing-feature gap, not a relay-key bug,
and needs its own change in insurance-strategist.html /
insurance-executive-portal.html and bpo-strategist.html /
bpo-executive-portal.html.
---
 html/war-rooms/bpo-war/bpo-war-room.html                | 5 +++--
 html/war-rooms/construct-war/construction-war-room.html | 5 +++--
 html/war-rooms/insure-war/insurance-war-room.html       | 5 +++--
 html/war-rooms/legal-war/legal-war-room.html            | 5 +++--
 html/war-rooms/re-war/re-war-room.html                  | 5 +++--
 5 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

